        "title": "Interaction of waves and currents with kelp forests (<i>Macrocystis pyrifera</i>): Insights from a dynamically scaled laboratory model",
        "id": "https://openalex.org/W2114070444",
        "cited_by_count": 42
      },
      "description": "These papers center on the biophysical ecology of kelp forests, asking how waves, currents, and turbulence interact with kelp morphology to shape both organism performance and the surrounding flow environment. They use a combination of field measurements, numerical/hydrodynamic modeling, and dynamically scaled laboratory experiments to quantify drag, force transmission, reconfiguration, particle and spore transport, and canopy-mediated mixing. Together, they treat kelp not just as passive habitat-formers but as flexible engineers whose mechanics alter local hydrodynamics and whose survival and ecological effects depend on that fluid–structure coupling."
    },
