        "id": "https://openalex.org/W2995337561",
        "cited_by_count": 1
      },
      "description": "These studies focus on kelp forests as foundation ecosystems whose structure, productivity, and persistence are strongly shaped by physical forcing and disturbance. Using a mix of long-term field monitoring, hydrodynamic measurements, manipulative removal experiments, historical surveys, and meta-analysis, they examine how waves, currents, storms, and climate-driven oceanographic regimes affect kelp demography, community succession, habitat function, and ecosystem services such as wave attenuation. Taken together, they link the ecology of canopy-forming kelps to both bottom-up environmental variability and the broader physical role kelp beds play in coastal systems."
