        "title": "Wave exposure influences kelp morphological and biomechanical phenotypic plasticity",
        "id": "https://openalex.org/W4402794739",
        "cited_by_count": 3
      },
      "description": "These papers collectively examine how kelps survive in mechanically stressful coastal habitats by linking morphology, tissue material properties, and hydrodynamic loading. Using field surveys, comparative biomechanics, scaling analyses, and experiments across wave-exposure gradients, they show that kelps adjust blade shape, stipe structure, and tissue strength plastically with size, season, and local flow conditions, and that damage from herbivores or encrusting invaders can weaken these defenses. Together, they frame kelps as flexible “engineering” organisms whose performance and survival depend on the interaction between growth form and the physical environment."
    },
